# EtSettingsToggleCard

A presentational settings card with a primary on/off toggle and an optional
action row that is revealed only while the toggle is on.

## When to use

A settings group that pairs a single boolean toggle (title + supporting
subtitle) with a follow-up action that is only relevant once the toggle is
enabled — e.g. "Advanced view" + "Manage columns". Originally extracted to
de-duplicate the identical card in the portfolio and watchlist settings sheets.

## API

| Prop                       | Type                          | Notes                                                    |
| -------------------------- | ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| `title`                    | `string`                      | Heading next to the toggle.                              |
| `subtitle`                 | `string`                      | Supporting copy under the heading.                       |
| `value`                    | `boolean`                     | Controlled toggle state.                                 |
| `onValueChange`            | `(value: boolean) => void`    | Fired on toggle.                                         |
| `action`                   | `EtSettingsToggleCardAction?` | Revealed row, shown only while `value` is `true`.        |
| `style`                    | `StyleProp<ViewStyle>`        | Outer card override — keep margins at the call site.     |
| `accessibilityLabel`       | `string?`                     | Card container label.                                    |
| `toggleAccessibilityLabel` | `string?`                     | Defaults to `title`.                                     |
| `toggleAccessibilityHint`  | `string?`                     | Defaults to `subtitle`.                                  |
| `testID` / `toggleTestID`  | `string?`                     | Toggle row / switch test ids.                            |

`EtSettingsToggleCardAction`: `{ label; onPress?; iconName? (default 'nut'); testID? }`.

## Notes

- Dumb/themeable: reads `cardDefault`, text, and `dividerQuinary` via
  `useEtoroTheme`; all copy, values, and handlers come from props.
- Margins are intentionally NOT baked in — pass `style` for spacing so each
  host sheet controls its own layout.
- Built from kit primitives: `EtText`, `EtToggleSwitch`, `EtListItem`, `EtIconV2`.
